   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 260 of the laws of 1969, relating to incorporating the\nPound Ridge Volunteer Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association and providing\nfor its powers and duties, in relation to updating such association's charter",
    "basePrintNo": "S5994",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5994-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1 - 4 & 7, Chap 260 of 1969",
    "lawSection": "Firefighters' Benevolent Association",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5994\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 260 of the laws of 1969, relating to incorporat-\ning the Pound Ridge Volunteer Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association\nand providing for its powers and duties, in relation to updating such\nassociation's charter\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nTo update the Pound Ridge Volunteer Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Associ-\nation's charter\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends sections 1, 2, 3, 4, and 7 of chapter 260 of the laws\nof 1969 to update the name of the association and description of persons\neligible for membership; to modernize and expand the purposes and duties\nof the association; and to expand permissible use of foreign fire insur-\nance monies by the association to actions \"in furtherance of its\npurpose.\"\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nVolunteer firefighters perform dangerous duties every day in our commu-\nnities, protecting our health, well-being and property. The Pound Ridge\nVolunteer Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association receives foreign fire\ninsurance premium tax monies from the New York State Insurance Depart-\nment. Currently, the association is authorized to use such funds only\nfor the care and relief of disabled or indigent volunteer and exempt\nfirefighters and their families. This legislation would authorize the\nAssociation to use the funds in furtherance of all its statutory\npurposes.\n\nThis act would amend the chapter of law governing the operation of the\nPound Ridge Volunteer Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association, in a\nmanner similar to recent legislative updates to other volunteer fire-\nfighters' benevolent association charters, so that it may more effec-\ntively work to support the health and well-being of the association, its\nmembers, and their families.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
